Subject: [PATCH 07802/11362] [outer-loop] ARC loop iter17: diagnose E3 'hang'
 = 600s LLM HTTP wait (test-isolation, not prod bug); process-killer is NOT
 the conductor

faulthandler probe located it: degenerate-frame test -> next_move ->
_induce_and_plan -> execute_bounded_llm_reinduction -> generate -> real
urllib.urlopen(timeout=self.timeout=600). proposer=None is the LIVE default
(_proposer() builds Qwen3.5-9B, timeout 600 intentional per 'eval has no time
limit'). So the test makes a real 600s HTTP call -> exceeds the 120s pytest
limit -> SIGTERM 143. NOT infinite, NOT a prod bug, NOT outer-loop-caused. Also
confirmed the carnot-orphan-cleanup janitor only kill -9's >120-MINUTE python and
never touched my seconds-old sweeps -- the conductor/watchdog was never the
killer, so it was left running. Test-isolation fix options recorded for operator.

